.TH MDT.RECOVERY_DELAY 4 2026-08-23 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
recovery_delay \- per-client recovery phase delays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdt." TARGET ".exports." NID ".recovery_delay"
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param obdfilter." TARGET ".exports." NID ".recovery_delay"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT or OST target client export
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B recovery_delay
parameter reports, for one specific client export, how many seconds after the
start of the most recent recovery that client completed each of the three
recovery phases. A phase the client never reached reports the string
.BR never .
Because all three delays are measured from the start of recovery, the time the
client spent inside request replay is
.B req_replay_delay
minus
.BR reconnect_delay ,
and the time spent in lock replay is
.B lock_replay_delay
minus
.BR req_replay_delay .
.PP
This is useful for isolating a specific client's recovery delay,
which is otherwise shown only in aggregate form in the full
.BR mdt.recovery_histogram (4)
or in limited numbers in
.BR mdt.recovery_top (4).
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.exports.*.recovery_delay
.B obdfilter.*.exports.*.recovery_delay
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the recovery delays for a client after a recovery:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param -n mdt.*.exports.10.0.0.7@tcp.recovery_delay"
reconnect_delay: 47
req_replay_delay: 61
lock_replay_delay: 64
.EE
Show a client that never finished lock replay:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param -n mdt.*.exports.10.0.0.9@tcp.recovery_delay"
reconnect_delay: 12
req_replay_delay: 30
lock_replay_delay: never
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B recovery_delay
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" commit v2_17_53
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.recovery_histogram (4),
.BR mdt.recovery_top (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8)
